# futex_mutex_counter.tkr — the §10 (plano-s10-multithread-nativo §6.2 / §8 T3) futex-mutex fixture
# (C backend). It proves the raw one-word futex mutex `mtx_lock`/`mtx_unlock` — built purely in Teko
# over the new `teko::sys::atomic_cas_u32`/`atomic_xchg_u32` intrinsics (M2/R5) and the `SYS_FUTEX`
# wait/wake syscall — provides real mutual exclusion under contention. WORKERS=8 threads each perform
# ITERS=10000 increments of ONE shared 64-bit counter, every increment held under the mutex; the
# threads share the counter through a single anonymous mmap page (a scalar address copied across the
# spawn boundary). The main thread waits (bounded poll on an atomic completed-worker word) for all
# eight to finish, then checks the counter equals WORKERS*ITERS = 80000. A racy (non-excluding) mutex
# would drop increments and the total would fall short. All increments serialized -> exit 0.
#
# The threads are spawned on the CURRENT (pthread) `spawn` substrate: the futex mutex is independent
# of how a thread was created, so this validates the M2 sync leaf ahead of the M3 raw-clone flip.

Feature: futex_mutex_counter — a raw futex mutex gives real mutual exclusion across contending threads

  Scenario: eight_workers_each_increment_ten_thousand_times_under_the_lock — no increment is lost
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
